1
00:00:01,835 --> 00:00:03,237
EPISODE 10

2
00:00:24,424 --> 00:00:26,527
Excuse me, you dropped this.

3
00:00:26,593 --> 00:00:28,161
I threw it away.

4
00:00:28,228 --> 00:00:31,098
Why throw away what's still inside?
What a waste.

5
00:00:31,164 --> 00:00:32,232
Just because.

6
00:00:32,299 --> 00:00:34,635
Why? Can't I throw it away?

7
00:00:35,769 --> 00:00:37,704
Wait.

8
00:00:51,318 --> 00:00:52,986
Then…

9
00:00:56,390 --> 00:00:58,325
can I keep this?

10
00:00:58,392 --> 00:01:00,961
Yes, sure.

11
00:01:01,728 --> 00:01:04,631
You're welcome to it. Well, then…

12
00:01:15,676 --> 00:01:18,412
Su-yeon, run!

13
00:01:19,813 --> 00:01:21,949
No, no!

14
00:01:22,749 --> 00:01:25,018
-Hey!
-No, no!

15
00:01:25,085 --> 00:01:27,888
-What is this?
-Su-yeon, run!

16
00:01:27,955 --> 00:01:30,123
Su-yeon!

17
00:01:34,494 --> 00:01:37,064
-Driver, hurry! Drive!
-Hey!

18
00:01:37,130 --> 00:01:38,999
Hey, hey!

19
00:01:39,833 --> 00:01:43,070
Come on, seriously!

20
00:01:45,505 --> 00:01:46,974
What are you doing? Get him!

21
00:01:47,040 --> 00:01:48,909
Hey, security just showed up!

22
00:01:48,976 --> 00:01:50,777
Darn it, I lost her right there!

23
00:01:50,844 --> 00:01:53,680
Don't worry, I got the license plate.

24
00:01:58,051 --> 00:02:01,188
Gosh, a grown man sulking like that.

25
00:02:01,254 --> 00:02:03,156
I'll let him off the hook.

26
00:02:07,394 --> 00:02:11,365
KIM KKEUT-SUN'S 70TH PARTY

27
00:02:30,851 --> 00:02:33,720
Where did these pretty boys come from?

28
00:02:33,787 --> 00:02:36,156
Here, I'm in a good mood!

29
00:02:37,591 --> 00:02:39,893
Oh my, look how fair your skin is.

30
00:02:40,694 --> 00:02:42,496
Goodness, you're so cute.

31
00:02:46,733 --> 00:02:49,369
All right, one, two, three.

32
00:02:51,505 --> 00:02:53,874
Auntie, please step in a little.

33
00:02:53,940 --> 00:02:56,977
And her daughter here, step in too.

34
00:02:57,778 --> 00:03:01,048
The big brother in back, step forward.

35
00:03:01,114 --> 00:03:03,750
All right, I'm taking the picture.

36
00:03:03,817 --> 00:03:05,252
KIM KKEUT-SUN'S 70TH PARTY

37
00:03:05,318 --> 00:03:07,354
One, two, three.

38
00:03:18,065 --> 00:03:21,702
Guys, let's never forget

39
00:03:22,302 --> 00:03:24,171
the humiliation we suffered today.

40
00:03:24,738 --> 00:03:28,675
Let's put out our album and succeed.

41
00:03:30,410 --> 00:03:32,045
And…

42
00:03:32,579 --> 00:03:34,381
let's keep this

43
00:03:34,448 --> 00:03:37,150
our secret for the rest of our lives.

44
00:03:37,217 --> 00:03:41,822
Still, at least now
we can cover the field with plastic.

45
00:03:43,457 --> 00:03:44,891
Min-gi.

46
00:03:46,693 --> 00:03:48,662
Let's hurry and leave.

47
00:03:48,729 --> 00:03:50,964
I don't want to stay here.

48
00:03:51,031 --> 00:03:53,200
-Let's go.

49
00:03:57,871 --> 00:03:59,272
Let's go.

50
00:03:59,339 --> 00:04:03,343
Your remaining balance is 37,900 won.

51
00:04:06,813 --> 00:04:08,048
What was that?

52
00:04:08,782 --> 00:04:11,318
-What happened?
-Didn't you hit the brake?

53
00:04:17,457 --> 00:04:19,993
-Hey, this is a foreign car, right?
-Yes.

54
00:04:38,211 --> 00:04:40,013
The alcohol is kicking back in.

55
00:04:42,916 --> 00:04:45,552
Ma'am! Ma'am!

56
00:04:51,358 --> 00:04:52,692
Mi-yeong?

57
00:04:55,962 --> 00:04:57,964
Are you awake, honey?

58
00:05:00,467 --> 00:05:03,770
-Ma'am! Ma'am!
-This is driving me crazy.

59
00:05:03,837 --> 00:05:06,139
Why do I keep thinking of that dream?

60
00:05:06,206 --> 00:05:07,774
What do I do if you leave?

61
00:05:07,841 --> 00:05:11,378
I told you, I won't work anymore
unless you pay me more.

62
00:05:11,444 --> 00:05:14,114
Still, how can you quit so suddenly?

63
00:05:14,181 --> 00:05:16,283
Caring for an old man is hard enough.

64
00:05:16,349 --> 00:05:18,952
Does it make sense
to make me watch a kid too?

65
00:05:19,019 --> 00:05:20,887
Anyway, I can't do this anymore.

66
00:05:20,954 --> 00:05:24,191
Pay me more or find someone else.
Figure it out yourself.

67
00:05:24,791 --> 00:05:26,793
Ma'am! Ma'am!

68
00:05:28,728 --> 00:05:33,166
-Mi-yeong, what's wrong?
-Sang-deuk, um, well…

69
00:05:34,467 --> 00:05:38,205
She's Dad's caregiver,
and she says she's quitting suddenly.

70
00:05:38,839 --> 00:05:42,175
I left the shop unattended too.
I'm going crazy here.

71
00:05:42,242 --> 00:05:44,010
Then should I watch him for you?

72
00:05:44,077 --> 00:05:46,646
No, how could I impose on you?

73
00:05:46,713 --> 00:05:49,115
It's fine. I've got nothing to do.

74
00:05:49,182 --> 00:05:51,785
Be back by five.
I do Three steps, one bow today.

75
00:05:52,519 --> 00:05:55,121
Oh, today's the day.

76
00:05:55,188 --> 00:05:58,992
But looking after Dad and Eun-u
won't be easy for you.

77
00:05:59,059 --> 00:06:02,596
How hard could it be to watch
an old man and one kid?

78
00:06:02,662 --> 00:06:04,564
Don't worry. Go on ahead.

79
00:06:04,631 --> 00:06:07,634
Thanks, Sang-deuk.
I'll be back as soon as I can.

80
00:06:08,568 --> 00:06:09,936
Be careful.

81
00:06:10,003 --> 00:06:11,838
Maybe I should even sell my car.

82
00:06:20,013 --> 00:06:23,283
What is with this house?

83
00:06:29,289 --> 00:06:30,857
How have you been, sir?

84
00:06:31,524 --> 00:06:34,461
Sir, it's me, Sang-deuk.

85
00:06:34,527 --> 00:06:36,263
Don't you remember me?

86
00:06:37,998 --> 00:06:40,400
-Ooh.
-Ooh?

87
00:06:41,768 --> 00:06:43,203
Ooh.

88
00:06:44,271 --> 00:06:45,939
Milk?

89
00:06:47,540 --> 00:06:49,943
-Pee.
-What?

90
00:06:51,444 --> 00:06:52,746
What is this?

91
00:06:53,480 --> 00:06:57,117
Isn't this pee? Gosh, you peed a lot.

92
00:07:01,087 --> 00:07:02,155
Oh, man.

93
00:07:02,222 --> 00:07:04,858
Why do you keep tearing all that up?

94
00:07:09,162 --> 00:07:10,897
Who are you, mister?

95
00:07:11,631 --> 00:07:15,268
Huh? Your mom asked me
to stay here with you today.

96
00:07:15,335 --> 00:07:18,071
Really? Then feed me,
with sausages on the side.

97
00:07:18,138 --> 00:07:22,475
Sausages? Okay, sure. Just a second.

98
00:07:24,311 --> 00:07:27,614
What? I fried the sausages. Eat up.

99
00:07:27,681 --> 00:07:30,583
I won't eat it.
It's not shaped like an octopus.

100
00:07:31,184 --> 00:07:32,152
An octopus?

101
00:07:32,218 --> 00:07:34,955
I won't eat sausages
unless they're octopus-shaped!

102
00:07:35,021 --> 00:07:37,424
Okay, okay, just wait a second.

103
00:07:37,490 --> 00:07:39,826
I'll make them octopus-shaped for you.

104
00:07:39,893 --> 00:07:41,995
She's so darn picky for a little kid.

105
00:07:43,630 --> 00:07:45,565
-Poo.
-Poo?

106
00:07:45,632 --> 00:07:46,633
Poo.

107
00:07:47,801 --> 00:07:50,136
-Pardon?
-Poop!

108
00:07:50,904 --> 00:07:52,572
Ugh, that smell!

109
00:07:55,508 --> 00:07:58,945
La, la, la

110
00:07:59,879 --> 00:08:01,548
Hey!

111
00:08:02,415 --> 00:08:05,218
-Su-yeon!
-Hand over my money, quick.

112
00:08:06,052 --> 00:08:08,088
How could I have money now, you brat?

113
00:08:08,154 --> 00:08:11,491
I have no time to argue with you now.
Just hand it over!

114
00:08:21,735 --> 00:08:25,772
Why are you doing this?
What is this all about?

115
00:08:25,839 --> 00:08:28,241
Where did you drop this woman off?

116
00:08:28,308 --> 00:08:31,711
I told you, I don't have any money.

117
00:08:31,778 --> 00:08:33,480
Will you keep repeating that?

118
00:08:33,546 --> 00:08:35,448
What can I do if I have no money!

119
00:08:35,515 --> 00:08:37,417
Then I have no choice.

120
00:08:40,687 --> 00:08:43,356
Hello, is this the police station?

121
00:08:44,324 --> 00:08:45,892
A bar here sells fake liquor,

122
00:08:45,959 --> 00:08:47,894
and I'd like to report it.

123
00:08:48,461 --> 00:08:49,696
Yes.

124
00:08:49,763 --> 00:08:52,298
The address here is…

125
00:08:55,101 --> 00:08:58,238
Okay, I'll give it to you, you bitch!

126
00:09:10,950 --> 00:09:12,819
Should've paid when I asked nicely.

127
00:09:12,886 --> 00:09:14,754
You always make me get vicious.

128
00:09:14,821 --> 00:09:16,956
You were always a vicious bitch.

129
00:09:17,023 --> 00:09:18,858
I just keep forgetting that.

130
00:09:18,925 --> 00:09:20,560
Thanks, I'm going!

131
00:09:24,998 --> 00:09:27,700
Where are you going? We need to talk.

132
00:09:29,536 --> 00:09:30,937
Let go of me!

133
00:09:31,004 --> 00:09:32,972
Who are you? Who are you people?

134
00:09:33,039 --> 00:09:35,942
Come with us quietly
if you don't want to get hurt.

135
00:09:40,880 --> 00:09:43,783
Hey, you black weasels!

136
00:09:52,492 --> 00:09:54,994
-You…
-Why are you so surprised?

137
00:09:55,061 --> 00:09:57,964
Didn't I tell you
I'm nothing without loyalty?

138
00:09:58,731 --> 00:10:01,367
What are you doing? Run now, you brat!

139
00:10:02,435 --> 00:10:03,536
Thank you so much!

140
00:10:22,222 --> 00:10:24,190
Screw you! Kiss my bra pads!

141
00:10:30,563 --> 00:10:32,298
There, do you like it now?

142
00:10:32,365 --> 00:10:33,933
It's so-so.

143
00:10:34,000 --> 00:10:35,268
So it's all done now?

144
00:10:35,335 --> 00:10:37,170
You have to color it too.

145
00:10:37,237 --> 00:10:38,805
Hurry up, please.

146
00:10:38,872 --> 00:10:42,142
Sure, I was about to do that anyway.

147
00:10:42,208 --> 00:10:45,378
A person has to finish well, you know,

148
00:10:45,445 --> 00:10:47,347
for the hard work to really show.

149
00:10:48,014 --> 00:10:49,315
Wait, this…

150
00:10:50,083 --> 00:10:51,651
what is this?

151
00:10:52,418 --> 00:10:53,820
Nothing's coming out.

152
00:10:53,887 --> 00:10:55,688
Just color it red, please.

153
00:10:55,755 --> 00:10:58,625
How can I color a tree frog red?

154
00:10:58,691 --> 00:11:00,026
It's not a poison frog.

155
00:11:00,093 --> 00:11:03,263
What can I do? I'm all out of green.

156
00:11:03,329 --> 00:11:06,132
I heard your mom has lots of money.

157
00:11:06,199 --> 00:11:08,134
She won't buy you colored pencils?

158
00:11:08,201 --> 00:11:09,769
My mom doesn't have money.

159
00:11:09,836 --> 00:11:12,205
-What?
-My mom's business went under.

160
00:11:12,272 --> 00:11:15,308
We had nowhere left to live,
so we moved down here.

161
00:11:16,409 --> 00:11:18,545
What are you doing? Hurry and color!

162
00:11:19,212 --> 00:11:22,515
Right, I'll do it. I was about to.

163
00:11:24,384 --> 00:11:25,818
I can't believe it.

164
00:11:25,885 --> 00:11:28,254
You're so impatient. Look at this.

165
00:11:28,321 --> 00:11:31,958
It looks poisonous now.
If it bites you, you'll die.

166
00:11:35,061 --> 00:11:37,430
I'm so sorry. I'm a bit late, right?

167
00:11:37,497 --> 00:11:39,799
No, not at all.

168
00:11:39,866 --> 00:11:41,734
I still have time anyway.

169
00:11:42,669 --> 00:11:46,005
-What about the shop?
-I left I-ji in charge.

170
00:11:47,440 --> 00:11:49,342
Today was rough on you, wasn't it?

171
00:11:49,409 --> 00:11:51,544
No, it was fine.

172
00:11:52,245 --> 00:11:54,948
Why are you so out of breath, though?

173
00:11:55,848 --> 00:11:58,218
Huh? Uh…

174
00:11:58,818 --> 00:12:00,753
I think I'm gaining belly fat,

175
00:12:00,820 --> 00:12:02,255
so I wanted to walk more.

176
00:12:02,322 --> 00:12:04,123
I… sold my car.

177
00:12:05,158 --> 00:12:06,759
Oh… did you?

178
00:12:06,826 --> 00:12:08,995
Well, I'll get going now.

179
00:12:09,062 --> 00:12:12,031
Thank you so much.

180
00:12:12,098 --> 00:12:14,234
I'll treat you later.

181
00:12:14,300 --> 00:12:15,969
No need.

182
00:12:25,111 --> 00:12:26,980
Oh, man…

183
00:12:27,547 --> 00:12:30,483
Mom, I used up all my colored pencils.

184
00:12:30,550 --> 00:12:32,518
Buy me some new ones.

185
00:12:32,585 --> 00:12:34,420
Okay, I'll buy you some.

186
00:12:34,487 --> 00:12:35,955
Darn it.

187
00:12:48,534 --> 00:12:50,003
We're back.

188
00:12:50,069 --> 00:12:51,871
Where have you all been?

189
00:12:51,938 --> 00:12:53,206
Huh?

190
00:12:53,273 --> 00:12:55,908
Why do you all look like that?

191
00:12:56,676 --> 00:12:59,045
We worked hard to save for the plastic.

192
00:12:59,112 --> 00:13:00,680
We lost it in a fender bender.

193
00:13:00,747 --> 00:13:03,116
What? A… fender bender?

194
00:13:03,182 --> 00:13:05,351
Yes, it was just a tiny scratch,

195
00:13:05,418 --> 00:13:07,920
but the estimate was a million won.

196
00:13:08,621 --> 00:13:10,690
It was so hard to save that money…

197
00:13:11,424 --> 00:13:12,725
Um, listen…

198
00:13:12,792 --> 00:13:14,894
"You said you'd never even talk to me."

199
00:13:14,961 --> 00:13:17,664
"So why are you talking to me now?"

200
00:13:18,331 --> 00:13:20,466
Tell her that for me, Ki-jun.

201
00:13:20,533 --> 00:13:21,634
Huh?

202
00:13:21,701 --> 00:13:23,970
She heard all that. You heard, Yun-hui?

203
00:13:26,873 --> 00:13:28,675
No, that's not it…

204
00:13:28,741 --> 00:13:31,344
Ask her if she can't see
I have a call, Ki-jun.

205
00:13:32,011 --> 00:13:33,680
Um, he says he has a call.

206
00:13:34,347 --> 00:13:36,082
Hello?

207
00:13:37,050 --> 00:13:39,986
Hi, Yu-na. What's up?

208
00:13:42,088 --> 00:13:43,523
That thing from before?

209
00:13:43,589 --> 00:13:45,491
It's nothing. Don't worry about it.

210
00:13:45,558 --> 00:13:47,593
Have you been eating well?

211
00:13:49,595 --> 00:13:52,231
Even if you're busy,
make sure you eat dinner.

212
00:13:57,470 --> 00:14:00,506
Jeez, jeez, seriously.

213
00:14:05,078 --> 00:14:07,747
I'm sure it's those guys from before.

214
00:14:07,814 --> 00:14:10,616
Why on earth are they chasing me?

215
00:14:11,284 --> 00:14:13,119
Something must've gone wrong.

216
00:14:18,191 --> 00:14:20,193
This is driving me crazy.

217
00:14:20,259 --> 00:14:22,128
Su-yeon!

218
00:14:24,831 --> 00:14:26,966
Are you okay? Were you really scared?

219
00:14:27,033 --> 00:14:30,103
Han-cheol, you haven't left yet?

220
00:14:30,169 --> 00:14:33,139
How could I leave you and go alone?

221
00:14:33,940 --> 00:14:35,875
But your face…

222
00:14:36,776 --> 00:14:39,345
I'm sorry. It's because of me.

223
00:14:39,412 --> 00:14:41,114
No, I'm fine.

224
00:14:41,180 --> 00:14:44,050
But are you sure you're really okay?

225
00:14:44,717 --> 00:14:46,652
Yes, thanks to you.

226
00:14:46,719 --> 00:14:50,289
I was so worried,
I thought I was going crazy.

227
00:14:52,325 --> 00:14:53,593
Han-cheol.

228
00:14:56,829 --> 00:15:00,066
I was just so worried that I…

229
00:15:00,133 --> 00:15:02,368
That's so embarrassing. I'm sorry.

230
00:15:05,371 --> 00:15:07,006
Thank you.

231
00:15:07,073 --> 00:15:08,408
For what?

232
00:15:08,474 --> 00:15:11,911
It's been so long
since anyone worried about me.

233
00:15:15,248 --> 00:15:18,484
By the way, who are those jerks?

234
00:15:19,752 --> 00:15:20,787
Pardon?

235
00:15:21,354 --> 00:15:23,823
Um, the thing is…

236
00:15:23,890 --> 00:15:25,425
It's okay, never mind.

237
00:15:25,491 --> 00:15:28,828
If it's hard to say, you don't have to.

238
00:15:28,895 --> 00:15:32,331
I'll protect you from now on.

239
00:15:34,934 --> 00:15:38,070
Let's go before those jerks come back.

240
00:15:38,137 --> 00:15:42,308
Actually, I'm curious about one thing.

241
00:15:42,375 --> 00:15:45,411
What does "bash your skull in" mean?

242
00:15:46,679 --> 00:15:49,649
Don't you dare show up
in front of my damn eyes again.

243
00:15:49,715 --> 00:15:52,518
Bother me one more time,
and I'll bash your skull in!

244
00:15:52,585 --> 00:15:55,488
I'll smash it to pieces, got it?

245
00:15:56,055 --> 00:15:57,089
Pardon?

246
00:16:00,326 --> 00:16:02,628
No, it's nothing.

247
00:16:03,296 --> 00:16:07,633
If she dumped me and left,
she could at least live well.

248
00:16:08,835 --> 00:16:11,204
What a foolish girl.

249
00:16:17,643 --> 00:16:19,045
Hey, you punk!

250
00:16:22,348 --> 00:16:23,783
Over here, you punk!

251
00:16:26,419 --> 00:16:30,389
What's this? Isn't this Min-gi's car?

252
00:16:31,390 --> 00:16:33,226
I took it over.

253
00:16:33,292 --> 00:16:34,694
It's Man-gu's now.

254
00:16:35,361 --> 00:16:37,964
Why drink before Three steps, one bow?

255
00:16:38,030 --> 00:16:39,999
I only had a little, man.

256
00:16:40,066 --> 00:16:42,201
A little, my foot…

257
00:16:42,969 --> 00:16:46,272
Yun-hui's raising hell
for you to hurry. Get in, quick.

258
00:16:50,743 --> 00:16:54,514
He only drives around fields all day.
A sports car, my foot…

259
00:16:55,114 --> 00:16:58,985
If you're jealous, just say so, punk.

260
00:17:02,522 --> 00:17:05,525
Hey, man, want to see something killer?

261
00:17:08,194 --> 00:17:10,796
Oh? The top's opening!

262
00:17:10,863 --> 00:17:13,766
Well? Killer, right? Killer, right?

263
00:17:13,833 --> 00:17:15,868
It's cold. Close it.

264
00:17:15,935 --> 00:17:18,070
You're such a bumpkin.

265
00:17:22,041 --> 00:17:24,844
Huh? Why's it doing this?

266
00:17:25,611 --> 00:17:28,047
What, it won't close?

267
00:17:28,114 --> 00:17:29,849
What's wrong with this thing?

268
00:17:29,916 --> 00:17:33,019
See, man? Why'd you even open the top?

269
00:17:37,890 --> 00:17:41,060
Mommy! Ow, it's hot!

270
00:17:41,127 --> 00:17:43,429
Hey, man, what are you doing?

271
00:17:43,496 --> 00:17:46,532
Mommy! Ow, it's hot!

272
00:17:46,599 --> 00:17:49,168
Jeez, watch the road and drive--

273
00:17:57,710 --> 00:17:59,645
Off to do Three steps, one bow?

274
00:17:59,712 --> 00:18:02,081
Yes, the Juyeop 2-ri representatives

275
00:18:02,148 --> 00:18:05,818
called to say they'll arrive
at the village in about an hour.

276
00:18:07,186 --> 00:18:09,188
Those guys said they'd come ages ago,

277
00:18:09,255 --> 00:18:11,023
so why are they still not here?

278
00:18:18,397 --> 00:18:21,801
-And Ki-jun and Hyeok?
-Said they were tired and went to bed.

279
00:18:21,867 --> 00:18:23,302
Already?

280
00:18:23,936 --> 00:18:26,739
Those guys must've been really shocked.

281
00:18:30,409 --> 00:18:32,345
Yes, hello?

282
00:18:33,145 --> 00:18:34,480
Yes, that's me.

283
00:18:36,182 --> 00:18:38,017
A car accident?

284
00:18:38,618 --> 00:18:42,588
Oh, no. Yes, yes,
I'll head right over there. Yes, yes.

285
00:18:42,655 --> 00:18:45,224
What do you mean? A car accident?

286
00:18:45,291 --> 00:18:48,094
They say Man-gu and Sang-deuk
got in a car accident.

287
00:18:48,160 --> 00:18:49,962
What? What?

288
00:18:51,197 --> 00:18:53,466
EMERGENCY MEDICAL CENTER

289
00:18:53,532 --> 00:18:55,301
-Oh, my goodness!
-Man-gu!

290
00:18:55,368 --> 00:18:56,702
Oh, no, Man-gu!

291
00:18:56,769 --> 00:18:58,771
How on earth did this happen?

292
00:18:58,838 --> 00:19:01,807
It's nothing. Just a little scratch.

293
00:19:03,109 --> 00:19:05,277
This is all your fault, you punk!

294
00:19:05,344 --> 00:19:07,680
-Hey, hey!
-What are you doing, mister?

295
00:19:07,747 --> 00:19:08,914
Hey, stop!

296
00:19:10,082 --> 00:19:13,419
That crappy car you sold me
put me in this pathetic state!

297
00:19:13,486 --> 00:19:15,655
-You punk!
-My car is not crappy.

298
00:19:15,721 --> 00:19:17,156
Your driving is crappy!

299
00:19:17,223 --> 00:19:18,691
What, you punk? Why, you…

300
00:19:18,758 --> 00:19:20,693
Cut it out already.

301
00:19:20,760 --> 00:19:23,763
By the way, where's Sang-deuk?

302
00:19:27,266 --> 00:19:29,068
Over there.

303
00:19:30,369 --> 00:19:32,138
-What's this?
-Huh?

304
00:19:33,172 --> 00:19:35,007
Is he unconscious?

305
00:19:36,709 --> 00:19:38,978
They say he's just drunk and asleep.

306
00:19:39,045 --> 00:19:40,379
No need to be alarmed.

307
00:19:42,048 --> 00:19:44,817
Still, it's a huge relief
that he isn't badly hurt.

308
00:19:44,884 --> 00:19:48,020
But what do we do
about Three steps, one bow?

309
00:19:48,087 --> 00:19:50,756
-Sorry about this, Yun-hui.
-Never mind.

310
00:19:50,823 --> 00:19:52,258
I'll have to do it alone.

311
00:19:52,324 --> 00:19:54,393
Alone? Didn't you say it takes two?

312
00:19:54,460 --> 00:19:56,696
Where would we find someone now?

313
00:19:56,762 --> 00:19:59,432
Plus, everyone here is elderly.
Who could do that?

314
00:19:59,498 --> 00:20:02,435
-Yeong-sik is right here.
-Me?

315
00:20:03,169 --> 00:20:07,506
You know I have a chronic slipped disc.

316
00:20:09,241 --> 00:20:11,177
Oh, right!

317
00:20:11,243 --> 00:20:14,714
Min-gi, you could just do it!

318
00:20:14,780 --> 00:20:17,817
Me? Why me? Am I crazy?

319
00:20:17,883 --> 00:20:19,885
All because you sold me a crappy car!

320
00:20:19,952 --> 00:20:21,253
My car isn't crappy.

321
00:20:21,320 --> 00:20:22,988
Your driving is what's crappy!

322
00:20:23,055 --> 00:20:24,690
Why, you little punk…

323
00:20:25,558 --> 00:20:28,294
Fine, then I'll make you

324
00:20:28,360 --> 00:20:30,596
an offer you can't refuse.

325
00:20:30,663 --> 00:20:35,568
If you finish Three steps, one bow,
I'll put it on for you.

326
00:20:36,235 --> 00:20:39,905
The plastic sheeting, no matter what.

327
00:20:45,177 --> 00:20:47,079
REVOKE RICE MARKET OPENING!

328
00:20:53,219 --> 00:20:57,223
Hey, have you two still not made up?

329
00:20:57,289 --> 00:20:59,358
Can't you two drop it already?

330
00:21:00,259 --> 00:21:04,730
Please tell her I'll forgive her
if she apologizes first, sir.

331
00:21:04,797 --> 00:21:06,398
Unbelievable.

332
00:21:08,367 --> 00:21:10,603
He says you should apologize first.

333
00:21:11,737 --> 00:21:14,540
"What did I do wrong
that I'd apologize first?"

334
00:21:14,607 --> 00:21:16,108
"Am I crazy?"

335
00:21:16,175 --> 00:21:19,445
Please tell him that, Uncle.

336
00:21:19,512 --> 00:21:21,080
Well, I mean…

337
00:21:22,248 --> 00:21:23,816
I don't know, forget it.

338
00:21:23,883 --> 00:21:25,417
Min-gi, you heard her too?

339
00:21:25,484 --> 00:21:28,687
"If you're going to quit halfway
and disgrace the town,

340
00:21:28,754 --> 00:21:30,990
don't even start in the first place!"

341
00:21:31,056 --> 00:21:33,893
Please tell him that too, Uncle.

342
00:21:33,959 --> 00:21:35,561
Seriously.

343
00:21:35,628 --> 00:21:38,097
"Please don't worry about others."

344
00:21:38,164 --> 00:21:41,500
Please tell her to just do
her own job properly,

345
00:21:41,567 --> 00:21:43,002
sir.

346
00:21:43,936 --> 00:21:47,339
Are you brats running me around
like a trained dog?

347
00:21:47,406 --> 00:21:49,108
You two sort it out yourselves.

348
00:21:49,742 --> 00:21:52,511
Hey, look, here they come!
Juyeop 2-ri is coming!

349
00:21:52,578 --> 00:21:53,679
Come on, let's go.

350
00:22:01,320 --> 00:22:03,055
Thank you for your hard work.

351
00:22:08,928 --> 00:22:10,663
-Ugh.
-We'll take it from here.

352
00:22:10,729 --> 00:22:13,299
We from Hadurok-ri will take over.

353
00:22:13,365 --> 00:22:15,835
-We're counting on you.
-Yes, of course.

354
00:22:16,468 --> 00:22:18,537
Three steps, one bow's final team,

355
00:22:18,604 --> 00:22:20,739
Hadurok-ri, has now taken the baton

356
00:22:20,806 --> 00:22:22,274
with the nation's hopes.

357
00:22:22,341 --> 00:22:25,411
Three steps, one bow will continue
to the county office.

358
00:22:26,078 --> 00:22:28,948
I hope the government hears
the farmers' earnest plea.

359
00:22:29,014 --> 00:22:31,650
To all our viewers watching online,

360
00:22:31,717 --> 00:22:34,019
we ask for your interest and support.

361
00:22:37,122 --> 00:22:38,858
-Ow, ugh.
-Ugh.

362
00:22:45,464 --> 00:22:48,167
-Ugh!
-Ow, ugh.

363
00:23:05,217 --> 00:23:07,152
Honey, are you okay?

364
00:23:07,219 --> 00:23:09,288
Yes, I'm okay.

365
00:23:10,189 --> 00:23:11,957
But why am I here?

366
00:23:12,024 --> 00:23:15,094
You were in an accident.
Don't you remember?

367
00:23:15,160 --> 00:23:17,396
That's right, I was.

368
00:23:18,163 --> 00:23:21,066
-And Man-gu?
-Barely hurt. He got treated and left.

369
00:23:21,133 --> 00:23:22,601
That's a relief.

370
00:23:23,402 --> 00:23:26,071
But why did you come here?

371
00:23:26,138 --> 00:23:30,376
How could I stay put after hearing
an accident put you in the hospital?

372
00:23:30,442 --> 00:23:33,846
What are you going to do
if someone from the village comes by?

373
00:23:33,913 --> 00:23:36,515
Sang-deuk!

374
00:23:36,582 --> 00:23:39,184
Grandpa!

375
00:23:40,019 --> 00:23:43,622
Quick, hide!
We're in big trouble if we're caught!

376
00:23:43,689 --> 00:23:45,724
What do I do? What do I do?

377
00:23:46,692 --> 00:23:48,727
Sang-deuk!

378
00:23:48,794 --> 00:23:51,330
Sang-deuk!

379
00:23:52,064 --> 00:23:53,632
Are you okay?

380
00:23:53,699 --> 00:23:55,034
Are you hurt badly?

381
00:23:55,100 --> 00:23:57,369
What? Yes, I'm fine.

382
00:23:57,436 --> 00:23:59,371
That's good, then.

383
00:24:02,541 --> 00:24:05,110
Why is it like this right here?

384
00:24:05,177 --> 00:24:07,112
Well, that's because…

385
00:24:07,980 --> 00:24:10,516
it's swollen. Really swollen.

386
00:24:10,582 --> 00:24:12,851
I took a huge direct hit to my side.

387
00:24:12,918 --> 00:24:14,119
Let me take a look.

388
00:24:14,186 --> 00:24:17,222
How badly did you get hurt
for it to swell up like this?

389
00:24:17,289 --> 00:24:18,557
No, don't!

390
00:24:19,291 --> 00:24:20,893
You startled me!

391
00:24:20,960 --> 00:24:23,062
Why scream like crazy, you rascal?

392
00:24:23,128 --> 00:24:25,431
It just looks too gruesome.

393
00:24:26,198 --> 00:24:27,866
It'd break your heart, Grandpa.

394
00:24:27,933 --> 00:24:29,168
Oh, dear.

395
00:24:29,768 --> 00:24:34,039
You're not even married yet,
and now you hurt your back too.

396
00:24:34,106 --> 00:24:36,909
Anyway, do you need anything?

397
00:24:36,976 --> 00:24:38,410
Well…

398
00:24:39,278 --> 00:24:42,614
I'm hungry.
Please go buy me some food, Grandpa.

399
00:24:42,681 --> 00:24:44,416
Something to eat?

400
00:24:46,251 --> 00:24:48,120
Want to eat this instead?

401
00:24:48,187 --> 00:24:50,022
Gosh, I'm not eating that.

402
00:24:50,089 --> 00:24:51,457
You kept sucking on that.

403
00:24:51,523 --> 00:24:53,325
Why keep telling me to eat it?

404
00:24:54,259 --> 00:24:56,428
It'd be a waste to throw it out.

405
00:24:58,063 --> 00:25:00,399
Then what do you want to eat?

406
00:25:01,233 --> 00:25:03,836
Porridge… Porridge, please.

407
00:25:03,902 --> 00:25:06,038
-Porridge?
-Abalone porridge.

408
00:25:06,105 --> 00:25:08,173
All right, got it.

409
00:25:09,875 --> 00:25:12,745
Please be careful and take your time.

410
00:25:12,811 --> 00:25:14,513
Okay, I will.

411
00:25:16,882 --> 00:25:19,485
Mi-yeong, come on out. Hurry.

412
00:25:20,252 --> 00:25:22,021
Come on, hurry!

413
00:25:49,481 --> 00:25:51,050
Repeal the open rice market!

414
00:25:51,116 --> 00:25:53,652
Repeal it! Repeal it!

415
00:25:53,719 --> 00:25:55,587
The government must wake up!

416
00:25:55,654 --> 00:25:57,823
Wake up! Wake up!

417
00:25:57,890 --> 00:25:59,758
Repeal the open rice market!

418
00:25:59,825 --> 00:26:01,894
Repeal it! Repeal it!

419
00:26:01,960 --> 00:26:04,263
The government must wake up!

420
00:26:04,329 --> 00:26:05,664
Let's rest for a bit.

421
00:26:05,731 --> 00:26:09,968
-Repeal the open rice market!
-Repeal it! Repeal it!

422
00:26:10,035 --> 00:26:14,273
-Repeal the open rice market!
-Repeal it! Repeal it!

423
00:26:14,339 --> 00:26:18,177
-The government must wake up!
-Wake up! Wake up!

424
00:26:18,243 --> 00:26:21,613
-Repeal the open rice market!
-Repeal it! Repeal it!

425
00:26:21,680 --> 00:26:26,085
-The government must wake up!
-Wake up! Wake up!

426
00:26:26,151 --> 00:26:27,786
Let's move aside. Move aside.

427
00:26:27,853 --> 00:26:30,089
Repeal it! Repeal it!

428
00:26:30,155 --> 00:26:32,291
A real woman only goes straight ahead.

429
00:26:32,357 --> 00:26:34,493
Repeal it! Repeal it!

430
00:26:34,560 --> 00:26:38,497
-The government must wake up!
-Wake up! Wake up!

431
00:26:38,564 --> 00:26:42,568
-Repeal the open rice market!
-Repeal it! Repeal it!

432
00:26:42,634 --> 00:26:46,538
-The government must wake up!
-Wake up! Wake up!

433
00:26:46,605 --> 00:26:50,275
-Repeal the open rice market!
-Repeal it! Repeal it!

434
00:26:50,342 --> 00:26:54,146
-Repeal the open rice market!
-Repeal it! Repeal it!

435
00:26:54,213 --> 00:26:58,650
-The government must wake up!
-Wake up! Wake up!

436
00:27:10,262 --> 00:27:11,497
Darn it!

437
00:27:21,740 --> 00:27:24,076
Min-gi, slow down a bit…

438
00:27:24,143 --> 00:27:26,311
Let go, darn it!

439
00:27:36,655 --> 00:27:38,824
Min-gi, let's rest a bit. Just a bit.

440
00:27:38,891 --> 00:27:40,592
Let go of me, darn it!

441
00:27:46,365 --> 00:27:49,768
This is really too hard on me, really!

442
00:27:58,644 --> 00:28:02,748
Fine, I'm sorry, you rotten bastard!

443
00:28:03,415 --> 00:28:06,785
But you just left without eating it.

444
00:28:10,689 --> 00:28:11,557
What?

445
00:28:11,623 --> 00:28:14,893
You asked for spaghetti, so I made it.

446
00:28:14,960 --> 00:28:17,596
And you just left to go to Yu-na.

447
00:28:18,163 --> 00:28:21,400
I worked so hard making that, darn it.

448
00:28:22,134 --> 00:28:24,169
So you made that spaghetti for me?

449
00:28:24,236 --> 00:28:28,473
You asked me to make it.
You said you wanted some.

450
00:28:29,341 --> 00:28:31,076
Just over that, you treated me…

451
00:28:31,143 --> 00:28:33,779
-That's why you were so cranky?
-Yes!

452
00:28:33,845 --> 00:28:36,281
And I even took out money for you

453
00:28:36,348 --> 00:28:38,984
because I wanted to lend it to you,

454
00:28:39,051 --> 00:28:41,286
but you had no idea how I felt, jeez!

455
00:28:45,457 --> 00:28:48,927
Wait, why bring this up
during Three steps, one bow?

456
00:28:48,994 --> 00:28:53,198
It's because you go so fast, you punk!

457
00:28:54,266 --> 00:28:56,501
Oh, come on.

458
00:29:05,310 --> 00:29:07,946
-Get up.
-Forget it, you jerk.

459
00:29:09,982 --> 00:29:11,416
All right.

460
00:29:11,483 --> 00:29:14,086
Okay, I'm sorry too. I'm sorry.

461
00:29:14,152 --> 00:29:16,555
Sorry for acting so childish.

462
00:29:16,622 --> 00:29:20,058
And I'm sorry
I didn't eat that spaghetti back then.

463
00:29:20,759 --> 00:29:22,894
Make it again. I'll really enjoy it.

464
00:29:22,961 --> 00:29:24,229
Forget it.

465
00:29:24,296 --> 00:29:26,331
I'll never do anything for you again.

466
00:29:26,398 --> 00:29:28,533
I really won't do anything!

467
00:29:29,901 --> 00:29:31,436
Okay, I get it.

468
00:29:31,503 --> 00:29:33,238
Hurry and get up.

469
00:29:33,305 --> 00:29:35,941
Want to shame Hadurok
before the whole country?

470
00:29:36,008 --> 00:29:37,042
Huh?

471
00:29:37,109 --> 00:29:38,744
We have to finish this.

472
00:29:40,746 --> 00:29:41,980
Come on, get up.

473
00:29:43,582 --> 00:29:45,484
Revoke the rice market opening!

474
00:29:45,550 --> 00:29:47,286
Revoke it! Revoke it!

475
00:29:52,991 --> 00:29:54,326
Come with me.

476
00:29:54,393 --> 00:29:55,994
Never mind.

477
00:29:57,529 --> 00:30:01,466
This is really too hard for me.

478
00:30:14,012 --> 00:30:15,414
Okay.

479
00:30:16,615 --> 00:30:18,317
Let's go together.

480
00:30:21,320 --> 00:30:22,554
Let's go.

481
00:30:30,996 --> 00:30:33,265
-Su-yeon, are you hungry?
-A little.

482
00:30:33,332 --> 00:30:35,801
There's a pork bone soup place nearby…

483
00:30:35,867 --> 00:30:37,402
Pork bone soup?

484
00:30:37,469 --> 00:30:39,938
You don't like food like that, do you?

485
00:30:40,005 --> 00:30:42,474
No, I really love it.

486
00:30:42,541 --> 00:30:45,210
But I'll pay for it.

487
00:30:45,277 --> 00:30:46,812
Really?

488
00:30:46,878 --> 00:30:49,181
I'm buying since you worried about me.

489
00:30:49,247 --> 00:30:52,250
Just don't get the wrong idea, okay?

490
00:30:52,851 --> 00:30:55,587
Yes, I got it.

491
00:30:55,654 --> 00:30:57,089
Shall we go?

492
00:31:03,095 --> 00:31:05,764
Today, local farmers opposed
the open rice market

493
00:31:05,831 --> 00:31:08,033
with a three-steps-one-bow march.

494
00:31:08,100 --> 00:31:11,269
Three steps, one bow ended
without any incident.

495
00:31:11,336 --> 00:31:15,407
After protesting the open rice market
in front of the county office,

496
00:31:15,474 --> 00:31:17,342
the farmers dispersed voluntarily.

497
00:31:19,911 --> 00:31:22,614
This Baekdudaegan National Arboretum

498
00:31:22,681 --> 00:31:24,850
is the largest in Asia,

499
00:31:24,916 --> 00:31:26,852
and has the world's second-largest

500
00:31:26,918 --> 00:31:28,620
seed research facility.

501
00:31:29,688 --> 00:31:33,225
We also collect
native and diverse plants

502
00:31:33,291 --> 00:31:36,828
and we study them
to develop new plant varieties.

503
00:31:37,496 --> 00:31:40,732
These plant varieties are
distributed to local residents,

504
00:31:40,799 --> 00:31:43,535
and the residents mass-produce them

505
00:31:43,602 --> 00:31:46,805
to sell for gardening or landscaping,

506
00:31:46,872 --> 00:31:49,040
earning a high profit.

507
00:31:49,107 --> 00:31:51,243
That concludes today's training.

508
00:31:51,309 --> 00:31:52,844
Thank you all for coming.

509
00:31:52,911 --> 00:31:54,813
Yes, thank you very much.

510
00:31:54,880 --> 00:31:56,114
Let's go, let's go.

511
00:31:56,181 --> 00:31:57,849
You're all just leaving?

512
00:31:58,383 --> 00:31:59,718
Why? Up for a drink?

513
00:31:59,785 --> 00:32:01,887
No, I've had plenty to drink.

514
00:32:01,953 --> 00:32:04,423
Want to go get a little refresher?

515
00:32:04,489 --> 00:32:05,757
It's on me.

516
00:32:09,995 --> 00:32:13,365
I even sold my car,
but I'm still strapped for cash.

517
00:32:13,965 --> 00:32:15,600
I'm in real trouble.

518
00:32:16,268 --> 00:32:18,103
Gosh…

519
00:32:21,973 --> 00:32:25,010
-What are you doing?
-Trying to develop a new menu item.

520
00:32:25,076 --> 00:32:28,647
A new menu item? Got anything in mind?

521
00:32:28,713 --> 00:32:32,117
Of course!
What's our town most famous for?

522
00:32:32,184 --> 00:32:33,785
Pine mushrooms, of course!

523
00:32:33,852 --> 00:32:35,821
Wild pine mushrooms meet coffee.

524
00:32:35,887 --> 00:32:37,923
A "Shroomericano." How's that?

525
00:32:37,989 --> 00:32:41,193
A… Shroomericano?

526
00:32:41,259 --> 00:32:43,261
But aren't those super expensive?

527
00:32:44,629 --> 00:32:47,032
About 300,000 to 400,000 won a kilo?

528
00:32:47,098 --> 00:32:49,501
And you want to put that in coffee?

529
00:32:49,568 --> 00:32:51,136
How much would you charge?

530
00:32:51,203 --> 00:32:53,371
Right, I guess that won't work.

531
00:32:53,438 --> 00:32:57,142
Then how about a sanghwang
mushroom latte? Is that pricey too?

532
00:32:57,976 --> 00:32:59,811
Why not an Udumbara Mocha?

533
00:33:00,612 --> 00:33:04,282
Ooh! Udumbara Mocha!
Udumbara Mocha, Udumbara Mocha!

534
00:33:04,349 --> 00:33:07,385
They say the coffee's best here.
Sit over there.

535
00:33:07,452 --> 00:33:08,887
Sang-deuk!

536
00:33:11,623 --> 00:33:14,893
-What brings you here?
-Uh, we had a training session today.

537
00:33:14,960 --> 00:33:17,963
These guys insisted on getting coffee.

538
00:33:18,029 --> 00:33:20,499
And give me five more coffees to go.

539
00:33:20,565 --> 00:33:22,267
-Five whole cups?
-Yes.

540
00:33:22,334 --> 00:33:25,003
I really love Americanos, actually.

541
00:33:25,070 --> 00:33:26,738
I drink them like water.

542
00:33:26,805 --> 00:33:28,907
Really? Okay, got it.

543
00:33:28,974 --> 00:33:30,609
I-ji, take their order.

544
00:33:30,675 --> 00:33:32,344
Yes, right away!

545
00:33:37,849 --> 00:33:40,085
Man-gu, is there any way to diversify

546
00:33:40,151 --> 00:33:42,587
our market project this time?

547
00:33:42,654 --> 00:33:46,491
It is a direct farmers market,
so having more items would be good.

548
00:33:48,059 --> 00:33:49,961
All settled with the Seoul office?

549
00:33:50,028 --> 00:33:52,964
I settled things
with the district office long ago.

550
00:33:53,031 --> 00:33:54,900
But what's a direct farmers market?

551
00:33:54,966 --> 00:33:58,203
We have a sister district office.

552
00:33:58,270 --> 00:34:00,338
Once a month, we sell crops grown here

553
00:34:00,405 --> 00:34:03,141
directly to consumers
at a farmers' market.

554
00:34:04,609 --> 00:34:07,312
Um… can we go to that too?

555
00:34:07,379 --> 00:34:08,880
You guys too?

556
00:34:09,581 --> 00:34:11,583
Do you guys have anything to sell?

557
00:34:11,650 --> 00:34:15,587
Of course we do!
Puffed beans and grasshoppers.

558
00:34:15,654 --> 00:34:17,656
-Wow!
-Well? Blows you away, right?

559
00:34:17,722 --> 00:34:20,559
-This, this has promise.
-Not bad, it has promise.

560
00:34:20,625 --> 00:34:22,561
-This, right?
-It'll work, it will!

561
00:34:22,627 --> 00:34:25,430
-Selling grasshoppers…
-Grasshoppers are everywhere.

562
00:34:25,497 --> 00:34:26,932
Mom.

563
00:34:28,099 --> 00:34:30,702
-Yes? What is it?
-Um, the thing is…

564
00:34:32,871 --> 00:34:34,639
It's nothing.

565
00:34:37,342 --> 00:34:39,210
Man-gu.

566
00:34:39,277 --> 00:34:40,979
Hello.

567
00:34:41,046 --> 00:34:44,049
Guys, would you like
to be on a show today?

568
00:34:50,589 --> 00:34:54,092
Is this all you meant
by being on a show?

569
00:34:54,159 --> 00:34:56,127
Are you looking down on my show?

570
00:34:56,194 --> 00:35:00,031
It may not look like it,
but I have over 1,000 regular viewers.

571
00:35:00,098 --> 00:35:01,766
Okay, let's do it for practice.

572
00:35:01,833 --> 00:35:04,135
What if your dad comes home
and sees this?

573
00:35:04,202 --> 00:35:07,872
-Your dad really hates us.
-It's fine, it's fine.

574
00:35:07,939 --> 00:35:10,375
My dad went fishing,
so he'll be home late.

575
00:35:13,345 --> 00:35:17,282
By the way, has your dad always…

576
00:35:17,349 --> 00:35:20,185
-been unable to speak?
-No.

577
00:35:20,251 --> 00:35:23,521
The ladies in town say
he could speak at first.

578
00:35:25,924 --> 00:35:28,660
Then what about your mom?

579
00:35:29,260 --> 00:35:31,062
I don't know.

580
00:35:31,129 --> 00:35:34,966
I heard Dad came to this village
alone with me before I turned one.

581
00:35:35,967 --> 00:35:37,602
Oh, no.

582
00:35:38,870 --> 00:35:41,673
What are you doing?
Aren't you getting ready?

583
00:35:41,740 --> 00:35:42,874
Okay.

584
00:35:48,947 --> 00:35:52,550
Whoa, it's an antique, a total antique.

585
00:35:52,617 --> 00:35:54,386
Oh, this?

586
00:35:54,452 --> 00:35:58,289
I first found this 17 years ago,

587
00:35:58,356 --> 00:36:00,191
so it must be way older.

588
00:36:00,258 --> 00:36:02,027
-You found it?
-Yes.

589
00:36:02,093 --> 00:36:04,429
On the hill behind town as a kid.

590
00:36:05,830 --> 00:36:08,967
This guy is why I got into music.

591
00:37:53,505 --> 00:37:57,475
After that, I spent all day
glued to just this guitar.

592
00:37:59,377 --> 00:38:02,514
Maybe I got too attached to this guy,

593
00:38:02,580 --> 00:38:05,750
-but I can't switch to another guitar.
-Who was that guy?

594
00:38:05,817 --> 00:38:08,319
No idea. It's been so long,
I barely remember.

595
00:38:09,087 --> 00:38:12,056
Anyway, that guy is my idol.

596
00:38:12,123 --> 00:38:15,660
I'd really love to meet him again…

597
00:38:22,333 --> 00:38:25,170
I told you to call. Why haven't you?

598
00:38:25,236 --> 00:38:27,972
You're really going to regret this.

599
00:38:28,039 --> 00:38:30,675
From your slightly angry big bro Viper.

600
00:38:32,510 --> 00:38:35,914
Alright, shall we start the show?

601
00:38:44,856 --> 00:38:48,393
MATILDA

602
00:38:48,459 --> 00:38:49,661
ANCKSUMUN: HI, MATILDA!

603
00:38:49,727 --> 00:38:51,996
They say first love is sad…

604
00:38:52,063 --> 00:38:55,733
because you love
with your heart, not your head.

605
00:38:55,800 --> 00:38:58,403
SINGLE12: I LOVE YOU
WITH MY HEART TOO, MATILDA

606
00:38:58,469 --> 00:39:00,038
REDNUT: TAKE ME, BABE!

607
00:39:00,104 --> 00:39:03,541
That's why I'm so sad again today.

608
00:39:03,608 --> 00:39:05,009
REDNUT: DON'T BE SAD
SINGLE12: FIRST LOVE? WHAT?

609
00:39:06,177 --> 00:39:08,646
You're asking who my first love is?

610
00:39:08,713 --> 00:39:10,615
REDNUT: WHO'S YOUR FIRST LOVE?

611
00:39:10,682 --> 00:39:12,016
It's all of you.

612
00:39:12,083 --> 00:39:14,419
ANCKSUMUN: TAKE ME, MATILDA!

613
00:39:14,485 --> 00:39:17,255
So today…

614
00:39:17,322 --> 00:39:19,924
just for all of you,

615
00:39:19,991 --> 00:39:22,594
I invited a special guest.

616
00:39:23,161 --> 00:39:24,696
Who is it, you ask?

617
00:39:24,762 --> 00:39:28,967
The ones who rocked Hongdae
seven years ago,

618
00:39:29,634 --> 00:39:31,336
the universe's best rock band,

619
00:39:31,402 --> 00:39:33,571
Excellent Souls!

620
00:39:33,638 --> 00:39:35,406
Come on out!

621
00:39:36,007 --> 00:39:37,508
ANCKSUMUN: WHAT? WHO'S COMING?

622
00:39:37,575 --> 00:39:39,611
REDNUT: WHO'S COMING FROM HONGDAE?

623
00:39:42,046 --> 00:39:45,283
-Wow!
-Say hi, say hi, say hi!

624
00:39:46,284 --> 00:39:49,888
-Hello, we're Excellent…
-Excellent Souls!

625
00:39:53,358 --> 00:39:56,561
Now, shall we hear a song first?

626
00:39:56,628 --> 00:40:00,598
-All together, let's go!
-Here goes.

627
00:40:00,665 --> 00:40:02,567
JUJUBETREE: KICK THOSE GUYS OUT!

628
00:40:02,634 --> 00:40:05,703
IMHUMAN: MY EARS ARE ROTTING!
MY EARS! MY EARS! MY EARS!

629
00:40:05,770 --> 00:40:07,171
JESSICAALBA HAS LEFT CHAT

630
00:40:07,238 --> 00:40:09,641
60SERVINGS: I ONLY CAME TO SEE MATILDA

631
00:40:09,707 --> 00:40:12,310
JESSICAALBA HAS LEFT CHAT
ANCKSUMUN HAS LEFT CHAT

632
00:40:24,489 --> 00:40:26,658
CHARISMAHONG: WHAT THE HECK IS THAT?

633
00:40:26,724 --> 00:40:29,594
ANCKSUMUN HAS LEFT CHAT
ROBBEDAGAIN HAS LEFT CHAT

634
00:40:29,661 --> 00:40:31,596
ANCKSUMUN: THIS STREAM'S DOOMED

635
00:40:31,663 --> 00:40:33,364
SOYOU: WHAT'S BEHIND YOU?

636
00:40:33,431 --> 00:40:36,734
JUJUBETREE: IT'S HER DAD!
HER DAD HAS APPEARED!

637
00:40:36,801 --> 00:40:39,771
JUJUBETREE: MATILDA,
BEHIND YOU! BEHIND YOU!

638
00:40:39,837 --> 00:40:41,606
CHERRY: WHAT'S HER DAD HOLDING?

639
00:40:41,673 --> 00:40:44,609
IKNOW: MATILDA,
YOUR DEAR FATHER HAS ARRIVED

640
00:40:44,676 --> 00:40:46,010
Dad!

641
00:40:46,077 --> 00:40:48,746
GRETEL: ISN'T THAT A CARP? LOL
DINO2: HAHAHA

642
00:40:48,813 --> 00:40:52,483
IKNOW: THAT CARP SLAP IS INSANE!
JUJUBETREE: HAHAHA

643
00:40:52,550 --> 00:40:54,118
CHERRY: HAHAHA

644
00:40:54,185 --> 00:40:56,721
SOYOU: THIS IS CRAZY, LOL
I'M RECORDING IT ALL

645
00:40:56,788 --> 00:40:58,856
CHERRY: SQUIDS BEATEN WITH A CARP, LOL

646
00:40:58,923 --> 00:41:02,327
DINO2: EPIC, LOL!
CHERRY: MY STOMACH HURTS!

647
00:41:04,495 --> 00:41:08,433
MAN-GU'S PINE MUSHROOMS ARE THE BEST

648
00:41:08,499 --> 00:41:10,868
Um, Man-gu.

649
00:41:10,935 --> 00:41:14,238
-About this box packaging…
-What is wrong with the box?

650
00:41:14,305 --> 00:41:17,542
Do you really have to slap this photo
on here like this?

651
00:41:17,608 --> 00:41:19,677
Who'd buy them if it puts them off?

652
00:41:19,744 --> 00:41:23,114
What's wrong with my photo?
It looks great to me.

653
00:41:24,282 --> 00:41:28,619
-Don't you think so, honey?
-I think it's so cute.

654
00:41:28,686 --> 00:41:31,990
But you look much better in person.

655
00:41:32,590 --> 00:41:33,791
Oh, stop it.

656
00:41:33,858 --> 00:41:36,894
You two have no shame
in front of your own mother!

657
00:41:36,961 --> 00:41:39,497
I've been so lonely lately as it is.

658
00:41:40,198 --> 00:41:42,533
Mom, do you have the autumn blues?

659
00:41:42,600 --> 00:41:45,503
I keep telling you to date
a nice man if you find one.

660
00:41:45,570 --> 00:41:47,538
Dating at my age? Forget it!

661
00:41:54,645 --> 00:41:57,181
How can that guy be like that?

662
00:41:57,248 --> 00:41:59,217
He's so shallow and ignorant.

663
00:41:59,884 --> 00:42:03,221
I can't date because I'm scared
of meeting a guy like that.

664
00:42:03,287 --> 00:42:05,323
Jeez…

665
00:43:36,547 --> 00:43:40,518
Eun-u, I'll carry your bag.
Give it here.

666
00:43:40,585 --> 00:43:42,320
I'm okay, though.

667
00:43:44,755 --> 00:43:46,124
Will you carry this then?

668
00:43:46,190 --> 00:43:48,292
No, I'll head out first.

669
00:43:52,797 --> 00:43:54,599
Give it here. I'll carry it.

670
00:43:56,434 --> 00:43:58,269
Min-guk!

671
00:44:01,472 --> 00:44:03,040
Did school just end?

672
00:44:03,107 --> 00:44:05,743
Min-guk, who's this foreign lady?

673
00:44:06,344 --> 00:44:07,845
You're Min-guk's friend.

674
00:44:07,912 --> 00:44:09,847
I'm Min-guk's mom.

675
00:44:09,914 --> 00:44:13,284
Really? Wow, that's so cool!

676
00:44:13,351 --> 00:44:15,453
Is your mom a foreigner?

677
00:44:16,354 --> 00:44:19,624
You hungry, Min-guk? Let's hurry home.

678
00:44:20,391 --> 00:44:22,226
Who's that? Your grandpa?

679
00:44:22,293 --> 00:44:24,095
Gosh, I'm Min-guk's dad!

680
00:44:24,162 --> 00:44:26,197
His dad! Father!

681
00:44:26,264 --> 00:44:30,001
Father? Really? Oh my god!

682
00:44:31,536 --> 00:44:33,204
I'll get going now.

683
00:44:33,771 --> 00:44:36,641
-Okay, take care.
-Bye!

684
00:44:36,707 --> 00:44:38,342
Let's go, Min-guk.

685
00:44:44,782 --> 00:44:47,418
-Min-guk!

686
00:44:47,985 --> 00:44:49,387
Wait, Min-guk!

687
00:44:52,156 --> 00:44:53,791
Min-guk!

688
00:44:55,993 --> 00:44:58,496
Min-guk, what is it?
Did I do something wrong?

689
00:44:58,563 --> 00:44:59,830
I don't know!

690
00:45:04,969 --> 00:45:08,206
Father Participation Class?
One-Day Guest Teacher?

691
00:45:08,272 --> 00:45:11,075
So they want me to teach
a class at his school.

692
00:45:11,142 --> 00:45:13,311
Sounds fun! Then I'll go watch too.

693
00:45:13,377 --> 00:45:15,446
-Sure.
-No, don't come!

694
00:45:15,513 --> 00:45:19,817
I'm embarrassed because the kids
tease me that you're a foreigner!

695
00:45:21,252 --> 00:45:24,689
Okay, I'll just head over by myself.

696
00:45:24,755 --> 00:45:26,023
Don't come either, Dad!

697
00:45:27,692 --> 00:45:28,559
Me too?

698
00:45:28,626 --> 00:45:32,797
The kids tease me,
saying you're my grandpa!

699
00:45:38,569 --> 00:45:40,404
A… grandpa?

700
00:45:40,471 --> 00:45:42,139
Me?

701
00:45:42,807 --> 00:45:44,141
Seriously.

702
00:45:44,208 --> 00:45:47,445
I feel like carp scales
are still coming off my body.

703
00:45:47,979 --> 00:45:51,282
How can you hit someone with a carp?

704
00:45:51,349 --> 00:45:54,051
I've heard of a kimchi slap,

705
00:45:54,118 --> 00:45:56,354
but a carp slap is a first for me.

706
00:45:57,855 --> 00:45:59,757
-Let's wash up.
-Hurry and wash up.

707
00:45:59,824 --> 00:46:02,827
-This hurts so much.
-I'm washing up too. It stings.

708
00:46:13,838 --> 00:46:15,373
Hey, little rock star.

709
00:46:15,439 --> 00:46:17,441
What are you looking at so closely?

710
00:46:17,508 --> 00:46:19,977
-Huh?
-It's nothing.

711
00:46:20,044 --> 00:46:21,612
No way it's nothing.

712
00:46:21,679 --> 00:46:23,347
What's this?

713
00:46:23,414 --> 00:46:24,649
DAD TEACHER DAY NOTICE

714
00:46:24,715 --> 00:46:25,850
A dad participation class?

715
00:46:26,717 --> 00:46:28,052
Please give it back.

716
00:46:28,119 --> 00:46:31,255
Please don't tell Mom about this.

717
00:46:32,456 --> 00:46:34,925
-Why?
-Please just don't.

718
00:46:34,992 --> 00:46:36,927
Promise me, okay?

719
00:46:37,561 --> 00:46:40,831
Okay, I got it.

720
00:46:47,638 --> 00:46:49,273
Su-yeon!

721
00:46:50,841 --> 00:46:52,543
Han-cheol.

722
00:46:52,610 --> 00:46:53,911
What brings you here?

723
00:46:53,978 --> 00:46:57,481
Now that we've made up,
we should go dig up sweet potatoes.

724
00:46:57,548 --> 00:47:01,152
You must really love sweet potatoes.

725
00:47:01,218 --> 00:47:02,920
It's freezing cold out here.

726
00:47:03,788 --> 00:47:05,189
-Yes.
-By the way,

727
00:47:05,256 --> 00:47:07,658
they're all dug up,
so none are left, right?

728
00:47:08,326 --> 00:47:09,827
What? Well, I suppose so.

729
00:47:09,894 --> 00:47:13,030
So I checked every
sweet potato field around here.

730
00:47:13,698 --> 00:47:17,101
There's still an unharvested
sweet potato field in Sangdurok-ri.

731
00:47:17,168 --> 00:47:20,204
Let's go. I'll lead the way. Come on.

732
00:47:30,448 --> 00:47:32,416
I'm so sorry. Let's go.

733
00:47:48,466 --> 00:47:50,000
What are you doing up?

734
00:47:50,067 --> 00:47:53,871
I still have some work to do
for the direct market sales.

735
00:47:54,572 --> 00:47:56,674
But why are you up and out here?

736
00:47:57,208 --> 00:47:58,509
I was thirsty.

737
00:48:03,547 --> 00:48:05,783
Um, listen.

738
00:48:05,850 --> 00:48:07,985
About Min-ho's dad…

739
00:48:10,955 --> 00:48:13,023
what was he like?

740
00:48:13,090 --> 00:48:15,659
-Why do you ask?
-I was just curious.

741
00:48:17,128 --> 00:48:19,797
I don't want to talk about it.
Just go to bed.

742
00:48:19,864 --> 00:48:21,899
Understood.

743
00:48:31,375 --> 00:48:33,878
Um, listen, well…

744
00:48:33,944 --> 00:48:36,514
-Min-ho…
-What about Min-ho?

745
00:48:38,382 --> 00:48:40,818
Never mind. Good night.

746
00:48:55,633 --> 00:48:57,301
Gotcha! Caught another one!

747
00:48:59,270 --> 00:49:01,005
I caught so many.

748
00:49:01,071 --> 00:49:03,941
-Don't wave that! Someone'll get hurt.
-No one will.

749
00:49:04,008 --> 00:49:06,777
This is seriously so annoying.

750
00:49:07,678 --> 00:49:10,748
Hey! What are you doing over there?

751
00:49:10,815 --> 00:49:12,783
Stop catching grasshoppers and work!

752
00:49:12,850 --> 00:49:15,052
Hey, this is work too, man.

753
00:49:15,119 --> 00:49:17,888
We're short on grasshoppers
for the farmers' market.

754
00:49:17,955 --> 00:49:19,657
That's just a side job.

755
00:49:19,723 --> 00:49:23,561
Shouldn't you finish your main job
before worrying about a side job?

756
00:49:24,962 --> 00:49:28,132
Jeez, I was about to catch one more.

757
00:49:28,199 --> 00:49:29,633
I'm coming up.

758
00:49:30,701 --> 00:49:32,803
Darn, I need to catch more of these.

759
00:49:32,870 --> 00:49:34,505
Oh, shoot!

760
00:49:40,277 --> 00:49:43,614
Why so shocked? That happy to see me?

761
00:49:44,849 --> 00:49:46,717
Who are those guys?

762
00:49:46,784 --> 00:49:50,154
Oh! The way to Sangdurok-ri?

763
00:49:50,221 --> 00:49:51,922
You just go that way.

764
00:49:51,989 --> 00:49:54,325
Are they asking for directions?

765
00:49:54,391 --> 00:49:56,961
-Are they your friends?
-Yes, sir.

766
00:49:57,027 --> 00:49:58,829
You embarrassed? Huh?

767
00:49:58,896 --> 00:50:01,799
Then why ghost my texts, you bastard,

768
00:50:01,866 --> 00:50:03,901
and make me pay to come all this way?

769
00:50:03,968 --> 00:50:05,803
Am I right or not?

770
00:50:05,870 --> 00:50:08,973
The vibe looks a little sketchy.

771
00:50:09,039 --> 00:50:12,009
What were you thinking,
blowing off my texts like that?

772
00:50:12,076 --> 00:50:15,913
Well, I… I was just so busy farming…

773
00:50:15,980 --> 00:50:19,884
Farming? A farmer?

774
00:50:19,950 --> 00:50:22,786
How could a loser like you farm?

775
00:50:22,853 --> 00:50:24,154
Why farming?

776
00:50:24,221 --> 00:50:27,291
I'm growing cabbages to… pay you back.

777
00:50:27,358 --> 00:50:29,193
You've got to be kidding me.

778
00:50:31,829 --> 00:50:34,164
You're either a genius
or an idiot, huh?

779
00:50:34,231 --> 00:50:37,368
I've seen guys steal to pay me back,

780
00:50:37,434 --> 00:50:39,803
and I've seen plenty pull scams.

781
00:50:39,870 --> 00:50:43,173
You're the first to grow cabbages
to pay back 100 million won.

782
00:50:43,240 --> 00:50:46,343
Boys, he said cabbages. Cabbages!

783
00:50:47,478 --> 00:50:50,648
Sorry for laughing so much
when you're being so serious.

784
00:50:50,714 --> 00:50:52,650
This won't do.

785
00:50:52,716 --> 00:50:55,019
We'll just have to do surgery, huh?

786
00:50:55,085 --> 00:50:57,388
Boys, we better get the tools ready.

787
00:50:57,454 --> 00:50:59,423
-Yes, sir.
-Wait a second!

788
00:51:00,157 --> 00:51:02,726
You said you'd spare my life!

789
00:51:03,861 --> 00:51:06,597
Fine, since a promise is a promise.

790
00:51:06,664 --> 00:51:09,934
But you know what happens
if you miss the deadline?

791
00:51:10,000 --> 00:51:11,101
Huh?

792
00:51:12,570 --> 00:51:14,572
Let's go now.

793
00:51:19,109 --> 00:51:22,513
Yes! Just head straight that way, sir!

794
00:51:22,580 --> 00:51:25,049
The air out here is fantastic.

795
00:51:25,115 --> 00:51:27,051
Feels like it's cleansing my lungs.

796
00:51:27,117 --> 00:51:28,919
Give me a cigarette.

797
00:51:31,522 --> 00:51:33,090
This jerk, seriously…

798
00:51:39,797 --> 00:51:42,032
No way, it couldn't be…

799
00:51:45,836 --> 00:51:47,805
Hey, who were those guys earlier?

800
00:51:47,871 --> 00:51:49,440
Do you happen to know them?

801
00:51:49,506 --> 00:51:50,841
Huh?

802
00:51:50,908 --> 00:51:53,644
No, they just asked for directions…

803
00:51:55,212 --> 00:51:57,948
What are you doing over there?

804
00:51:58,015 --> 00:52:00,551
It's nothing.

805
00:52:01,852 --> 00:52:04,888
But why do you look so down?

806
00:52:05,823 --> 00:52:08,025
Well, uh, you see.

807
00:52:08,092 --> 00:52:11,562
Honestly, let me ask you one thing.

808
00:52:13,797 --> 00:52:16,266
How old do I look?

809
00:52:18,669 --> 00:52:20,838
-Thirty-two, sir.
-You little punk!

810
00:52:22,606 --> 00:52:25,609
Stop flattering me and be honest.

811
00:52:25,676 --> 00:52:28,112
-I won't get mad.
-Fifty-nine, sir.

812
00:52:28,178 --> 00:52:31,982
Fifty-nine?
Hey, you punk, I'm 40! Forty!

813
00:52:32,716 --> 00:52:34,351
You said you wouldn't get mad.

814
00:52:34,418 --> 00:52:37,655
I even shaved off five or six years.

815
00:52:39,790 --> 00:52:42,326
Why do you ask that all of a sudden?

816
00:52:43,761 --> 00:52:47,064
My son says he's embarrassed
because I look like a grandpa.

817
00:52:48,298 --> 00:52:50,234
Oh, kids that age can be like that.

818
00:52:50,300 --> 00:52:51,802
At that age…

819
00:52:51,869 --> 00:52:54,872
Honestly, what you have
comes along once in a century.

820
00:52:54,938 --> 00:52:56,306
It's congenital old face.

821
00:52:56,373 --> 00:52:59,877
Plus, since your style doesn't help,

822
00:52:59,943 --> 00:53:02,946
you start off looking
at least ten years older.

823
00:53:03,013 --> 00:53:05,249
-What?
-And here's the worst part.

824
00:53:05,315 --> 00:53:09,987
The biggest problem is
that dated Choi Jae-bong hairstyle.

825
00:53:10,721 --> 00:53:13,223
-My hairstyle?
-Yes.

826
00:53:16,627 --> 00:53:18,729
How would you like your hair, sir?

827
00:53:18,796 --> 00:53:22,066
First, please straighten out
those crunchy ramen noodles.

828
00:53:23,200 --> 00:53:25,569
What do you mean? Why straighten it?

829
00:53:25,636 --> 00:53:28,505
I paid a whole 20,000 won for this
a few days ago!

830
00:53:30,140 --> 00:53:33,177
Dear customer, is that a waste
when you'll look younger?

831
00:53:33,243 --> 00:53:34,812
If you'd rather not, fine.

832
00:53:34,878 --> 00:53:38,248
No, no, I'll do it. I'll do it, okay?

833
00:53:38,916 --> 00:53:40,117
That's right.

834
00:53:40,184 --> 00:53:42,019
Just sit tight and get ready.

835
00:53:44,188 --> 00:53:45,889
This style looks great.

836
00:53:46,724 --> 00:53:49,860
Please make it just like this photo.

837
00:53:51,595 --> 00:53:55,999
Uh, well… I'll give it a try.

838
00:54:00,904 --> 00:54:03,073
I kind of want to change my hair color.

839
00:54:03,140 --> 00:54:04,475
That's not the problem.

840
00:54:04,541 --> 00:54:07,678
One wrong move,
and he might not teach us how to farm.

841
00:54:07,745 --> 00:54:10,981
Still, it's amazing the country
has a beauty shop like this.

842
00:54:11,048 --> 00:54:12,683
Salon.

843
00:54:17,955 --> 00:54:19,790
When on earth will this be over?

844
00:54:23,293 --> 00:54:25,829
That style isn't exactly a quick fix.

845
00:54:26,797 --> 00:54:28,499
How is it?

846
00:54:31,835 --> 00:54:34,538
It feels kind of awkward to me.

847
00:54:35,272 --> 00:54:37,708
Why did I spend 100,000 won on this?

848
00:54:38,342 --> 00:54:40,177
Does it really look okay?

849
00:54:40,244 --> 00:54:41,979
Uh, of course! Right now…

850
00:54:42,679 --> 00:54:44,515
you look a good 20 years younger!

851
00:54:44,581 --> 00:54:46,483
Quit exaggerating, kid…

852
00:54:47,017 --> 00:54:49,853
If it looked weird,
I was going to kill you guys.

853
00:54:52,055 --> 00:54:54,858
Looking again, I reckon it's not bad.

854
00:55:00,764 --> 00:55:02,232
This is serious.

855
00:55:02,299 --> 00:55:04,101
I think we took it too lightly.

856
00:55:04,168 --> 00:55:06,770
Hey, we have to bluff no matter what.

857
00:55:06,837 --> 00:55:09,006
Insist it looks great on him, got it?

858
00:55:09,072 --> 00:55:11,308
It really looks great on you.

859
00:55:11,875 --> 00:55:13,877
It's the exact look you wanted.

860
00:55:13,944 --> 00:55:15,312
Nice.

861
00:55:20,918 --> 00:55:23,020
Is the farmers market prep going well?

862
00:55:23,086 --> 00:55:24,354
Yes.

863
00:55:24,421 --> 00:55:26,824
But what made you buy everyone coffee?

864
00:55:26,890 --> 00:55:29,193
You hardly ever drink coffee.

865
00:55:29,259 --> 00:55:30,260
Huh?

866
00:55:30,327 --> 00:55:32,663
Uh, well, the thing is…

867
00:55:32,729 --> 00:55:35,699
I just started liking coffee lately.

868
00:55:35,766 --> 00:55:40,537
Well now, for a country boy,
you sure know good coffee.

869
00:55:42,406 --> 00:55:45,609
-Take a break and have a snack.
-Hold on a second.

870
00:55:46,677 --> 00:55:48,512
A snack?

871
00:55:48,579 --> 00:55:50,480
Wait, did you actually cook?

872
00:55:50,547 --> 00:55:54,518
Yes, it's my masterpiece. Get ready.

873
00:55:54,585 --> 00:55:56,720
Ta-da!

874
00:55:57,754 --> 00:56:02,092
Uh… Honey, can I ask what this is?

875
00:56:02,159 --> 00:56:04,561
This? It's a ramen bar.

876
00:56:04,628 --> 00:56:06,964
A… ramen bar?

877
00:56:07,030 --> 00:56:09,900
Some is always left when I make ramen.

878
00:56:09,967 --> 00:56:14,171
I hated to waste it, so I froze it.

879
00:56:16,273 --> 00:56:19,543
It looks tasty, right? Go on, try it.

880
00:56:19,610 --> 00:56:21,245
Uh, this is…

881
00:56:35,292 --> 00:56:38,028
Still, uh… elders should come first.

882
00:56:38,095 --> 00:56:40,464
I can't be so rude and eat first.

883
00:56:41,365 --> 00:56:42,466
Excuse me…

884
00:56:43,233 --> 00:56:46,770
Sir, please have some of this.

885
00:56:48,505 --> 00:56:50,374
Sir?

886
00:56:51,141 --> 00:56:53,176
Come on, sir!

887
00:56:53,243 --> 00:56:56,380
I know you're pretending to sleep.

888
00:56:56,446 --> 00:56:59,349
What is everyone doing here?

889
00:57:00,617 --> 00:57:02,119
Man-gu?

890
00:57:02,185 --> 00:57:04,321
What the hell did you do to your head?

891
00:57:04,388 --> 00:57:06,657
Shut up if you don't know anything.

892
00:57:06,723 --> 00:57:10,694
This is the Kim Soo-hyun style,
the hottest look right now, punk!

893
00:57:10,761 --> 00:57:13,897
It only looks good on Kim Soo-hyun.

894
00:57:14,665 --> 00:57:17,534
-Does it look that weird?
-Is that even a question?

895
00:57:17,601 --> 00:57:20,437
I'm afraid it'll give me nightmares.

896
00:57:20,504 --> 00:57:22,506
It's fine, it's totally fine.

897
00:57:22,572 --> 00:57:25,375
They're just not used to it yet.

898
00:57:25,442 --> 00:57:27,811
-Phew.
-Exactly, that's right.

899
00:57:27,878 --> 00:57:30,747
The first day of a haircut
is always awkward, right?

900
00:57:30,814 --> 00:57:33,116
-That's right.
-It's always like that.

901
00:57:33,183 --> 00:57:34,851
What's with your hair suddenly?

902
00:57:34,918 --> 00:57:38,021
I'll be a guest teacher
at Min-guk's school in a few days.

903
00:57:38,088 --> 00:57:40,724
-That's why I made an effort.
-A guest teacher?

904
00:57:40,791 --> 00:57:42,659
The school's having a dads' class.

905
00:57:42,726 --> 00:57:44,594
You and I are on the same day…

906
00:57:46,463 --> 00:57:47,731
You didn't know?

907
00:57:47,798 --> 00:57:49,566
Didn't Min-ho tell you?

908
00:57:49,633 --> 00:57:51,568
Min-ho never mentioned that.

909
00:57:54,004 --> 00:57:57,574
Could Min-ho be embarrassed
because he doesn't have a dad?

910
00:57:57,641 --> 00:57:58,775
That bastard!

911
00:57:58,842 --> 00:58:01,011
Hey, what are you talking about, huh?

912
00:58:01,078 --> 00:58:03,780
He probably just forgot.

913
00:58:03,847 --> 00:58:05,816
Gosh, I better hurry home.

914
00:58:05,882 --> 00:58:07,851
Min-guk will love this, right?

915
00:58:07,918 --> 00:58:10,087
He'll go, "Dad!"

916
00:58:28,505 --> 00:58:30,173
Min-guk, what's wrong?

917
00:58:30,240 --> 00:58:32,376
I don't look like a grandpa now.

918
00:58:32,442 --> 00:58:35,379
Now you look like a crazy grandpa!

919
00:58:35,445 --> 00:58:37,014
A crazy grandpa?

920
00:58:37,080 --> 00:58:39,049
You just don't know any better.

921
00:58:39,116 --> 00:58:42,419
This is the latest trend,
the Kim Soo-hyun movie style.

922
00:58:42,486 --> 00:58:45,889
Forget it! You and Mom embarrass me.

923
00:58:45,956 --> 00:58:48,025
Don't even come near my school!

924
00:58:53,563 --> 00:58:55,532
It's the Kim Soo-hyun movie style…

925
00:58:58,535 --> 00:59:00,103
A crazy grandpa?

926
00:59:02,939 --> 00:59:05,675
I'm the crazy bastard, I am!

927
00:59:05,742 --> 00:59:08,578
I'm the crazy bastard
for believing those punks!

928
00:59:08,645 --> 00:59:11,715
Those little bastards, I swear!

929
00:59:15,552 --> 00:59:18,155
Honey, what's wrong?

930
00:59:18,221 --> 00:59:19,322
Are you crying?

931
00:59:19,389 --> 00:59:20,891
Wait, why?

932
00:59:22,125 --> 00:59:24,928
I feel so sorry to Min-guk.

933
00:59:28,198 --> 00:59:31,234
I'm sorry I'm an embarrassing mom.

934
00:59:32,602 --> 00:59:35,138
You're not embarrassing at all…

935
00:59:44,014 --> 00:59:47,150
Oh, Min-ho, you're reading a book.

936
00:59:47,217 --> 00:59:48,718
You're back?

937
00:59:48,785 --> 00:59:50,587
-Yes.

938
00:59:50,654 --> 00:59:52,155
Um, Min-ho.

939
00:59:52,222 --> 00:59:55,559
Do you have anything to tell me?

940
00:59:56,326 --> 00:59:58,161
No, nothing. Why?

941
00:59:58,228 --> 01:00:00,664
Nothing, just asking.

942
01:00:00,730 --> 01:00:03,633
I'll go play at Wang-bae's house.

943
01:00:08,905 --> 01:00:11,208
Yun-hui, are you okay?

944
01:00:11,274 --> 01:00:13,910
I'm okay.

945
01:00:13,977 --> 01:00:16,646
He must be embarrassed too.

946
01:00:16,713 --> 01:00:18,748
If he told me, he knows I'd go,

947
01:00:18,815 --> 01:00:20,450
so that's probably why.

948
01:00:20,517 --> 01:00:23,053
Don't take it too hard.

949
01:00:23,120 --> 01:00:25,188
Kids that age are all like that.

950
01:00:25,255 --> 01:00:27,224
He's just a kid, just a kid.

951
01:00:37,634 --> 01:00:39,936
Hey, little rock star.

952
01:00:40,003 --> 01:00:42,272
Why are you here and not at Wang-bae's?

953
01:00:42,339 --> 01:00:44,207
No reason.

954
01:00:44,274 --> 01:00:48,445
What are you going to do
about the dads' open class?

955
01:00:50,046 --> 01:00:52,315
You're really not telling your mom?

956
01:00:54,784 --> 01:00:56,052
Why?

957
01:00:56,119 --> 01:00:58,054
Embarrassed she might go instead?

958
01:00:58,121 --> 01:01:01,558
Come on, kid.
A real man isn't embarrassed by that.

959
01:01:01,625 --> 01:01:03,727
That's not it.

960
01:01:04,494 --> 01:01:05,996
Then what is it?

961
01:01:06,062 --> 01:01:08,431
I'm afraid Mom will cry again.

962
01:01:09,533 --> 01:01:11,768
Whenever my dad comes up,

963
01:01:11,835 --> 01:01:16,506
my mom always cries alone in secret.

964
01:01:17,307 --> 01:01:22,012
I don't mind being teased,
but I hate it when Mom cries.

965
01:01:22,679 --> 01:01:25,715
I just don't want to upset her.

966
01:01:25,782 --> 01:01:30,554
So please keep it a secret too.

967
01:01:31,188 --> 01:01:33,490
Okay, I will.

968
01:01:40,597 --> 01:01:42,532
Yun-hui!

969
01:01:42,599 --> 01:01:46,002
What are you two talking about?

970
01:01:47,404 --> 01:01:49,039
It's nothing.

971
01:01:50,273 --> 01:01:53,109
You two must be sharing a secret.

972
01:01:53,977 --> 01:01:55,612
I'll get out of your way.

973
01:01:55,679 --> 01:01:57,247
Have fun talking, you two.

974
01:01:57,314 --> 01:01:59,783
I should go feed the cows.

975
01:02:28,211 --> 01:02:30,080
What are you doing?

976
01:02:30,814 --> 01:02:32,849
Can't you tell by looking?

977
01:02:32,916 --> 01:02:34,251
I'm feeding the cows.

978
01:02:35,518 --> 01:02:38,655
You heard what Min-ho said.

979
01:02:40,557 --> 01:02:42,325
Are you okay?

980
01:02:44,261 --> 01:02:45,895
I'm okay.

981
01:02:46,930 --> 01:02:49,866
I don't think
I deserve to be a mom either.

982
01:02:51,768 --> 01:02:54,170
While I was listening to Min-ho,

983
01:02:54,237 --> 01:02:57,941
I just felt upset and hurt by him.

984
01:03:00,377 --> 01:03:02,312
But it turns out my baby

985
01:03:03,079 --> 01:03:05,882
only did that out of worry for me.

986
01:03:07,017 --> 01:03:08,885
Yun-hui.

987
01:03:08,952 --> 01:03:10,654
I feel so guilty,

988
01:03:11,621 --> 01:03:13,290
and my heart breaks for him.

989
01:03:15,959 --> 01:03:18,161
Because I'm so ill-fated,

990
01:03:18,862 --> 01:03:21,631
my poor Min-ho has it so hard, Min-gi.
